(3186577, 442948, 69050, '<td valign="top">ya im not to proud of this lol, i took it the afternoon of the deadline (i didn''t take it FOR the challenge) but when i saw it i though... why not lol. I wasn''t expecting to win but i submitted it anyways cuz if i have it, why not right? Oh well, i just wanna get this out of the top 4 and forget about it haha. Faster shutterspeed would have been great but the duck did it so fast i didn''t have time to think :P</td>', 'ya im not to proud of this lol, i took it the afternoon of the deadline (i didn''t take it FOR the challenge) but when i saw it i though... why not lol. I wasn''t expecting to win but i submitted it anyways cuz if i have it, why not right? Oh well, i just wanna get this out of the top 4 and forget about it haha. Faster shutterspeed would have been great but the duck did it so fast i didn''t have time to think :P', '2007-01-05 21:23:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(3187033, 442690, 16230, '<td valign="top">The Falkirk Wheel is a fascinating structure and you certainly captured a nice view of the place. The composition and colors are great, but those reflections... Wow! Congratulations on your ribbon!</td>', 'The Falkirk Wheel is a fascinating structure and you certainly captured a nice view of the place. The composition and colors are great, but those reflections... Wow! Congratulations on your ribbon!', '2007-01-06 00:19:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(3188582, 442457, 28742, '<td valign="top">A bit dark or over contrasty to me. Having not read the image title, I stared at it thinking the round thing was a bowl of something. Different, interesting, but too much blackness, IMO to be a top contender. A 5.8 is pretty decent though. Woulda been a 6 from me. Hope this is useful.</td>', 'A bit dark or over contrasty to me. Having not read the image title, I stared at it thinking the round thing was a bowl of something. Different, interesting, but too much blackness, IMO to be a top contender. A 5.8 is pretty decent though. Woulda been a 6 from me. Hope this is useful.', '2007-01-06 14:18:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(3188615, 442457, 70, '<td valign="top">I always tell people that you really need to smack people in the face with the challenge topic. In this case, though, I think it''s almost overkill. Pattern for the sake of pattern with not much else. I agree with Wavelength, it''s a bit painful to look at.</td>', 'I always tell people that you really need to smack people in the face with the challenge topic. In this case, though, I think it''s almost overkill. Pattern for the sake of pattern with not much else. I agree with Wavelength, it''s a bit painful to look at.', '2007-01-06 14:30:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(3188707, 442457, 54540, '<td valign="top">This shot is very interesting to me technically - meaning I really like the way the marble is bending the screen from it''s weight.  Reminds me of the models that represent the bending of space and time.<br/> <br/>Artistically, if the subject, the marble, were fully in frame and lighter (brighter) than it is, perhaps looking like it was lit from the inside, I would easily give this shot a 7 or 8.  That would have added the needed ''wow'' punch for me.  As the shot is currently set up, I would have voted this a 6.<br/> <br/>Hope that helps!</td>', 'This shot is very interesting to me technically - meaning I really like the way the marble is bending the screen from it''s weight.  Reminds me of the models that represent the bending of space and time. Artistically, if the subject, the marble, were fully in frame and lighter (brighter) than it is, perhaps looking like it was lit from the inside, I would easily give this shot a 7 or 8.  That would have added the needed ''wow'' punch for me.  As the shot is currently set up, I would have voted this a 6. Hope that helps!', '2007-01-06 15:17:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(3188781, 442457, 33982, '<td valign="top">a number of interesting concepts - some of which i''ve tried (to much less success ;) <br/> <br/>my biggest problem with the image is the darkness of the marble  does not enhance the grid  but detracts from the whole pattern <br/>i really like the abstracts in the grid - and may have to investigate that futher myself ;)<br/></td>', 'a number of interesting concepts - some of which i''ve tried (to much less success ;)  my biggest problem with the image is the darkness of the marble  does not enhance the grid  but detracts from the whole pattern i really like the abstracts in the grid - and may have to investigate that futher myself ;)', '2007-01-06 15:50:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(3189519, 442656, 66182, '<td valign="top">renoire, ang akong comment ani as a critic, dili inamigo ba, is that you should have let your model a little bit "takilid" towards you to create a "2/3" angle to define more her beauty, features and to tell the viewer that she is sleeping. if im to look at the photo, murag naglili kog "dead". hehe. makahadlok instead nga makapagahi....mayo lang gani nagsuot ug nighties....</td>', 'renoire, ang akong comment ani as a critic, dili inamigo ba, is that you should have let your model a little bit "takilid" towards you to create a "2/3" angle to define more her beauty, features and to tell the viewer that she is sleeping. if im to look at the photo, murag naglili kog "dead". hehe. makahadlok instead nga makapagahi....mayo lang gani nagsuot ug nighties....', '2007-01-06 21:07:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(3193758, 442550, 32459, '<td valign="top">[<i>Yes, I am the culprit. To all those who are pained to see it. <br/>That was my sole objective, to bring to the notice the harsh realities of life (and death). <br/>Some of the members have called it a jocular title. I do not agree. First of all, I was short of words (in the title) for me to explain what I wanted to explain. Second, I did not want comments like the simple DNMC''s. Therefore, I declared in the title itself that it does not meet the challenge. <br/>Regarding the first part of the title, we all are made up of same pattern. This photograph represents someone who was born like us, but remained unknown. At least, with this photograph, I have been able to generate respect for the baby. <br/>I know, it is a disturbing, shocking, offensive, upsetting, immoral, gruesome, intriguing, sad, upsetting, disgusting and sick. <br/>But, I don''t agree that I have not shown respect for the baby. Perhaps he would have objected if he had a voice, but now he has his voice, through all of us!]</i> <br/> <br/>You know... as a passerby of this ''so-called'' side-show attraction, I would have the option of choosing to go in and view this sort of thing or not. With that, if I should choose to go in to see these "festivities," even if I knew nothing of the contents of the display before entering, I would have the choice to balk at such an unimaginable disrespect and disgusting exploitation of a human being. <br/> <br/>This "magic show" you shake your finger at is no worse than you are. You have chosen to use this media to illustrate whatever ridiculous point you''re trying to make here is, and you have subjected all of us (including the children who frequent this community) to it and your idiocy!  Due to the size of the thumbnail, virtually no one could have made out what this picture was without clicking on it WHILE under the impression that it was related to the challenge!<br/> <br/>So, what actually IS your point anyway? &lt;ahem&gt; "Don''t put stillborn deformed babies in jars and publicly display them!" Alright!  But a better chant here is this: Don''t FORCE us to view it! If your point was to illustrate how badly that baby was exploited, it was not done so as badly as you exploited it! <br/></td>', '[Yes, I am the culprit. To all those who are pained to see it. That was my sole objective, to bring to the notice the harsh realities of life (and death). Some of the members have called it a jocular title. I do not agree. First of all, I was short of words (in the title) for me to explain what I wanted to explain. Second, I did not want comments like the simple DNMC''s. Therefore, I declared in the title itself that it does not meet the challenge. Regarding the first part of the title, we all are made up of same pattern. This photograph represents someone who was born like us, but remained unknown. At least, with this photograph, I have been able to generate respect for the baby. I know, it is a disturbing, shocking, offensive, upsetting, immoral, gruesome, intriguing, sad, upsetting, disgusting and sick. But, I don''t agree that I have not shown respect for the baby. Perhaps he would have objected if he had a voice, but now he has his voice, through all of us!]  You know... as a passerby of this ''so-called'' side-show attraction, I would have the option of choosing to go in and view this sort of thing or not. With that, if I should choose to go in to see these "festivities," even if I knew nothing of the contents of the display before entering, I would have the choice to balk at such an unimaginable disrespect and disgusting exploitation of a human being.  This "magic show" you shake your finger at is no worse than you are. You have chosen to use this media to illustrate whatever ridiculous point you''re trying to make here is, and you have subjected all of us (including the children who frequent this community) to it and your idiocy!  Due to the size of the thumbnail, virtually no one could have made out what this picture was without clicking on it WHILE under the impression that it was related to the challenge! So, what actually IS your point anyway? <ahem> "Don''t put stillborn deformed babies in jars and publicly display them!" Alright!  But a better chant here is this: Don''t FORCE us to view it! If your point was to illustrate how badly that baby was exploited, it was not done so as badly as you exploited it! ', '2007-01-08 00:27:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(3193900, 442756, 46336, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings from the Critique Club. </b> <br/> <br/>Hi Helena, <br/> <br/>Welcome to DPC! Congratulations on your first challenge submission - that''s a big first step. <br/> <br/>This is a difficult one to critique as there is nothing technically wrong, and I don''t have much to go on in terms of your comments. The main issue here is one of composition. I recommend you take the time to read this tutorial on composition -&gt; <a href="//ronbigelow.com/articles/adv_comp/adv_comp.htm" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">here</a> <br/> <br/>Based on this shot there are thwo aspects that I believe you should begin to consider. The first is colour: these greys tend to make an image look flat, and don''t engage the voter. On DPC the voters usually like a nice bit of pop in the shots. The second is leadign lines: in this shot the pattern in the material leads the viewers eye right off the image, so there is no real focal point. <br/> <br/>It is my hope that these insights are helpful and constructive. Please feel free to PM me if you have any questions regarding this critique. And please remember to mark it "Helpful" if you found it so. Good luck with future challenges. <br/> <br/>Cheers<br/>Paul</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club.   Hi Helena,  Welcome to DPC! Congratulations on your first challenge submission - that''s a big first step.  This is a difficult one to critique as there is nothing technically wrong, and I don''t have much to go on in terms of your comments. The main issue here is one of composition. I recommend you take the time to read this tutorial on composition -> here  Based on this shot there are thwo aspects that I believe you should begin to consider. The first is colour: these greys tend to make an image look flat, and don''t engage the voter. On DPC the voters usually like a nice bit of pop in the shots. The second is leadign lines: in this shot the pattern in the material leads the viewers eye right off the image, so there is no real focal point.  It is my hope that these insights are helpful and constructive. Please feel free to PM me if you have any questions regarding this critique. And please remember to mark it "Helpful" if you found it so. Good luck with future challenges.  CheersPaul', '2007-01-08 00:49:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(3194038, 442457, 69050, '<td valign="top">wow i dont know why i didn''t notice this before! This should have won for sure! Fits the challenge perfectly, the colors are great, the technique is brilliant! i would have given this a 10 had i seen it. Faved.</td>', 'wow i dont know why i didn''t notice this before! This should have won for sure! Fits the challenge perfectly, the colors are great, the technique is brilliant! i would have given this a 10 had i seen it. Faved.', '2007-01-08 01:09:53.000000', NULL, 0),
