(3284784, 440767, 72142, '<td valign="top">You may have noticed that almost the entire face of your subject is hidden by bars and the like.  My suggestion in future situations, place a small mirror in the photo to permit viewing of the subject.  <br/> <br/>The date stamp, while informative, does not add to the artistic quality of the photo.  My suggestion, provide a calender or other date/time indicating device in the background of the photo if this information is crucial.  <br/> <br/>On a positive note, your subject seems to have a good attitude.</td>', 'You may have noticed that almost the entire face of your subject is hidden by bars and the like.  My suggestion in future situations, place a small mirror in the photo to permit viewing of the subject.   The date stamp, while informative, does not add to the artistic quality of the photo.  My suggestion, provide a calender or other date/time indicating device in the background of the photo if this information is crucial.   On a positive note, your subject seems to have a good attitude.', '2007-01-26 03:03:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(3301291, 442979, 62382, '<td valign="top">how did you light it?  am really curious.</td>', 'how did you light it?  am really curious.', '2007-01-29 23:24:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(3305042, 442927, 22301, '<td valign="top">Hey I have been on that bridge many times, long and flat! Congrats on your PB, although a bit late. I was just looking at your photo and noticed how small your file size,  31 kb, And you can use up to 150 kb. I think this is why your photo has the artifacts, because I don''t think ou should have any noise at ISO 50. I am not sure what software you use but whatever they have for Save for the Web or equivalent will strip the exif from the photo and allow a bigger file size.<br/>Congrats on 5th place!</td>', 'Hey I have been on that bridge many times, long and flat! Congrats on your PB, although a bit late. I was just looking at your photo and noticed how small your file size,  31 kb, And you can use up to 150 kb. I think this is why your photo has the artifacts, because I don''t think ou should have any noise at ISO 50. I am not sure what software you use but whatever they have for Save for the Web or equivalent will strip the exif from the photo and allow a bigger file size.Congrats on 5th place!', '2007-01-30 23:17:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(3327012, 441788, 73499, '<td valign="top">Beautiful.</td>', 'Beautiful.', '2007-02-04 18:31:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(3355363, 442481, 60862, '<td valign="top">This is a very nice capture.  I like the tilt, too.  I think with a bit more contrast it would''ve broken 6.  I would''ve voted it 6 as is.</td>', 'This is a very nice capture.  I like the tilt, too.  I think with a bit more contrast it would''ve broken 6.  I would''ve voted it 6 as is.', '2007-02-12 01:00:22.000000', NULL, 0),
